---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SISTER_HODINARIUM } from '../data/sites';
---
<Base
  title="English summary"
  description="Czech Horology Society (Český spolek horologický) — society of clock and tower-clock enthusiasts based in Czechia."
>
  <article class="en-doc" lang="en">
    <header class="en-header">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">English summary</p>
      <h1>Czech Horology Society</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        <strong>Český spolek horologický</strong> is a non-profit association of
        clock enthusiasts, restorers and craftspeople based in Czechia.
        We run the <em>Hodinárium</em> exhibition at Děčín Castle, restore
        historical tower clocks across the country, and operate a 200+ article
        online encyclopedia of horology.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="en-section">
      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <ul class="en-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Hodinárium Děčín</strong> — a permanent exhibition of clocks at the
          Děčín chateau in northern Bohemia: Black Forest clocks, electric clocks,
          mechanical regulators, and tower clock movements from the 15th century onwards.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Tower-clock restoration</strong> — identification, conservation
          and documentation of historical tower clock movements. Past projects
          include movements from Soběslav, Bychory, Janovice and others.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Online encyclopedia</strong> — over 200 articles on clockmaking
          on <a href={SISTER_HODINARIUM} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{`hodinarium-eu.pages.dev`}</a>,
          plus a dedicated specialised website on the Prague Astronomical Clock at
          <a href="https://orloj.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">orloj.eu</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Member meetings &amp; lectures</strong> — annual general assemblies
          and presentations by members on horology, restoration projects and
          DIY clockmaking.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="en-section">
      <h2>Formal details</h2>
      <dl class="en-dl">
        <div>
          <dt>Legal form</dt>
          <dd>Registered association (<em>spolek</em> per Czech Civil Code)</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Company ID (IČO)</dt>
          <dd>26573008</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Registered office</dt>
          <dd>nábřeží Otakara Ostrčila 273/6, 392 01 Soběslav III, Czechia</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Court registration</dt>
          <dd>L 4908 / Regional Court in České Budějovice (registered 2016-03-05)</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Predecessor</dt>
          <dd>Virtuální muzeum hodin o. s. (Virtual Clock Museum, registered 2009)</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="en-section">
      <h2>Mission statement</h2>
      <blockquote class="en-quote">
        The purpose of the association is to present and popularise the technical
        and artistic development of clocks from their earliest constructions to
        the present day. To promote interest in this field of cultural heritage
        we primarily use the possibilities of the Internet. We promote and
        popularise creative work in this field including small-scale and amateur
        clockmakers.
      </blockquote>
      <p class="cite-source">— from the association's articles</p>
    </section>

    <section class="en-section">
      <h2>Visit Hodinárium</h2>
      <p>
        The exhibition is open seasonally (April—October) at Děčín Castle in
        northern Bohemia, ~90 minutes from Prague by train. Up-to-date opening
        hours are on the
        <a href="https://www.zamekdecin.cz/vystavy/vystava-decinske-hodinarium" target="_blank" rel="noopener">castle's official site</a>
        or in the
        <a href={`${SISTER_HODINARIUM}/decin`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hodinárium → Děčín</a>
        section of our encyclopedia.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="en-section">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <ul class="en-list contact-list">
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:info@orloj.eu">info@orloj.eu</a></li>
        <li>Phone: <a href="tel:+420603502735">+420 603 502 735</a></li>
        <li>
          Web (Czech): <a href="/">horologie-cz.pages.dev</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="en-section en-licence">
      <h2>License</h2>
      <p>
        Texts on this site are published under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/deed.en" target="_blank" rel="license noopener">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International</a>.
        You may share and adapt the material with proper attribution.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .en-doc {
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .en-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-brass) 25%, transparent);
  }
  .en-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-brass-bright);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .en-section {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .en-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    color: var(--color-brass-bright);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .en-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .en-list li {
    padding: 0.6rem 0 0.6rem 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-brass) 15%, transparent);
    position: relative;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .en-list li::before {
    content: '·';
    color: var(--color-copper);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .en-list li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .contact-list li::before { content: ''; }
  .contact-list li { padding-left: 0; }

  .en-dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .en-dl {
      grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
      gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    }
    .en-dl div { display: contents; }
  }
  .en-dl dt {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    color: var(--color-copper);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .en-dl dd {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .en-dl dd { margin-bottom: 0; }
  }

  .en-quote {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-copper);
    padding: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .cite-source {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .en-licence p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
